To further test the relationship with source distance, we compared the N_{\\rm HGal}(Dickey & Lockman, 1990; Kalberla et al., 2005; Willingale et al., 2013) to the published1N_{\\rm H} for the 28 BH and NS XRBs with well estimated source distances2(Gandhi et al., 2018; Miller-Jones, 2014, and references therein). We find that in all cases but two (GRS 1915+105 and V4641 Sgr) the measured N_{\\rm H} was either below or comparable to the expected Galactic line-of-sight absorption for these systems.

